Word costs from the pyopenjtalk-plus dictionary
===============================================

data/ipadic-costs.tsv sets the word costs of IPADIC entries to the costs that the dictionary of
pyopenjtalk-plus 0.4.1.post10 (https://github.com/tsukumijima/pyopenjtalk-plus) gives the same
entries; scripts/data/buildJapaneseCosts.ts derives it. That dictionary is NAIST-jdic as customized
for Open JTalk, with vocabulary from UniDic-CSJ 2.2.0 and patches derived from mecab-ipadic-NEologd
(Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE-APACHE-2.0). pyopenjtalk-plus is under the MIT license of
pyopenjtalk below, and its dictionary under the licenses after that (its COPYING file, as
distributed with it).


